>The BA350 can be configured as either a single SCSI bus or it can be
>split into two separate SCSI busses.  In either case, the busses are
>terminated and do not daisy chain.
>
>When configured as a single bus, if the chassis is mounted horizontally
>with the power supply to the left, the topmost SCSI connector is used.
>
>When configured as a dual bus, the topmost connector connects slots 0,
>2, and 4.  The bottom connector connects slosts 1, 3, 5, and 6.
>
>To configure the chassis as a single bus, the jumper board (BA35X-MC) is
>installed behind slot 5 and the terminator board (BA35X-MB) is installed
>behind slot 1.  For a dual bus, swap these two items.
>
>Good luck!
>
