Kare,

The Celebris XL service maintenance manual states:

When the Pentium PCI Series CPU module has been installed, the
computer will support up to 192MB using 32MB SIMMs on SIMM banks 0
through 5.
The computer is shipped with at least 8MB of memory. 4MB, 8MB, 16MB,
32MB, or 64MB (future) single in-line memory modules (SIMMs) may be
added.
When installing SIMMs take care of the following:
� SIMMs must be installed in pairs. For example, a 32MB SIMM in bank 0
and a 32MB SIMM in bank
1. Different SIMM sizes can not be mixed within banks.
� SIMMs must be the same type, size, and speed.
� SIMMs must have an access time of 70 ns or less.

It doesn't state that the memory must be fast page mode, and that it
can be either parity or non-parity.  The Celebris XL Pentium processor
card has the Intel NX chipset on it.  The NX chipset requires fast
page mode memory, and it is not designed to work with EDO.

Also, I would not believe the bit about "64MB (future)".

