I recently picked up a ZLXp-L1 card at a nice price.  I decided to test 
it in my Alphastation 200-4/233 using OpenVMS V7.2 and Win NT V4.0sp3.
The regular card is the older ZLXp-E2 that came with the system.

Well, after locating the NT-alpha drivers and installing, I tried it
under NT and it works, and is somewhat (though not startlingly)
faster than the ZLXp-E2 card.  After getting VMS upgraded to V7.2-1
and installing Open3D (I wish the license for that was in the hobbyist 
kit...) it also worked well enough there.  But there's one _major_
annoyance I'm wondering about, and if its the card or themonitor (Nokia 
447L).

The monitor no longer seems to 'remember' being set up to properly 
display the screen; tested at 1280x1024:75, 1280x1024:72, and 
1024x768:72.  It loses the width/height/centering completely when
the monitor is turned off or when _anything_ causes a change in 
monitor output from the card (including logging on to Win-NT, using
the operators console under DECwindows (Motif) or running some NT
programs that change resolution).  This never happened 
with the ZLXp-E2 card (and no I haven't had time to switch back to 
retest, but I will tomorrow).  

Has anyone experienced wierdness like this from a -L1 card and what
is essentially a not-quite-cheap SVGA multisync monitor?  Its bad
enough to make me switch back to the -E2 card...

