Joe Smith wrote in message <3901edf0$0$209@nntp1.ba.best.com>...


>Nixie tubes had a neat feature.  The least significant digit was a bit
>analog.


Well, that's not a Nixie phenomenon, it happens with any counter
where the LSD is displayed.  Therer's always a +0 -1 count
error due to the time window not being in sync with the input signal.
You will get that flicker effect as the signal crosses over the range of the
LSD.

You can look at this as a "bug" or as you cleverly interpreted it,
a "feature".







