  KLESI, IIRC.

:an an RA82 hard drive (which connects by the SDI interface).

  Most commonly a UDA50 or (better, in this case) KDB50, or via 
  the CI, an HSC-series controller, and a BI-based CI adapter.

:Unfortunately, DEFBOO.COM and the related files on the console are
:configured to boot the machine using an HSC over an interface called
:the CI.

  The steps involved in booting the system are basically the same.
  Boot the console, EXIT from the console dead sergeant prompt, and 
  MC EDT the DEFBOO.CMD to do what you want.  The console filename 
  is usually something like DZ1:[CONSOLE]DEFBOO.COM or 
  LB0:[CONSOLE]DEFBOO.COM.  Then RUN CONTROL to restart the console.

  The three directories (relevent to this discussion) found out on the 
  Pro console disk are (IIRC) [8800], [8700], and [CONSOLE].  IIRC,
  you want the files in [CONSOLE] -- platform-specific files go into
  the other directories...  (Assuming you have a version circa 4 or
  later of the Pro console...)

  Poke around through the *BOO.COM files to see what they do...

:  Since the console came from a different unit, that's not
:surprising that it's configured to boot of a different device.  What I
:want to know is how to make the VAX boot off the disk (or the tape
:drive, if possible).  I believe that the hard drive may have an
:operating system on it, and if not, we have VMS (4.2, I think) on
:tape.  I'd be greatful for any info or boot-file examples you could
:offer.

  You've got a whole pile of them on your Pro disk...

  Get the console release notes -- the Pro console can do a fair 
  amount of work without the system being bootstrapped...

  Look in lb0:[console]release.* for some details...


 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
