The >>> prompt designates the SRM console, which is used to boot both OpenVMS
and Tru64 (aka Digital Unix, AKA OSF1) and which can be used for some of the
free Unix compatible OS'es such as Linux and the *BSD's.

At the >>> prompt try the command boot, if there is an installed OS, then the
system will boot and you will have a completely different set of questions to
come back and ask us.

If not then you need to aquire an OS.

There are hobbiest programs for both Tru64 and OpenVMS, and I'm sure you can find
details about them by asking another question here.

Information about the Unix Compatibles can be found at www.linux.org, www.netbsd.org,
www.freebsd.org and www.openbsd.org

You can also run WindowsNT  on this box although why you would want to is a mystery.

When you know which OS you have installed/want to install come back and we will be
able to give you lots more help.

Hope this helps
Adam Price

