people to break the traditions of usenet. For example when one first want's to post a
question, it is considered good form to read a while before you post, so that you have
a feel for the group, and know what sort of questions will fit in. By filtering the
messages you see to only include threads which stem from a CNET query they present
a distorted view of the group, which encourages people to post off topic.
