In article <panderson-DDD5D8.12050526042000@news.earthlink.net>, Paul 
Anderson <panderson@genicom.com> wrote:

> You can reset the network card to factory defaults with jumpers on the 
> network card, but I don't have a DEClaser 3500 manual handy to tell you 
> what jumper that is.

It's jumper 6.  Take the network card out of the printer, set jumper 6 
to ON and put the network card back in.  Do not connect it to the 
network.  Turn the printer on and let the card go through its powerup 
sequence.  When it's done (say 30 seconds to be safe) turn it off and 
return jumper 6 to OFF.  Now when you power on the printer again, it 
will have an IP address of 192.whatever which should be reachable on 
your network.

Paul

