Maybe that's because bulbs have a voltage / resistance characteristic which is
very non linear - square law IIRC. If you have ever used generators for
lighting, even a volt or two drop on the line is enough to produce noticeable
flicker.

This characteristic was used on many of the early valve / tube wien bridge audio
generators for amplitude stabilisation - worked pretty good too...

Chris



