Nixie tubes had a neat feature.  The least significant digit was a bit
analog.

For instance: a frequency meter with a Nixie tube display is connected
to an oscillator that is slowly drifting.  The display reads either
"17.4" or "17.5" kilohertz, and flickers rapidly back and forth between
those to digitial readings.  But the duty cycle varies.  The brightness
of the "5" digit starts low, and as it gets brighter, the "4" digit gets
dimmer.  Calling out the display to your lab partner, you could say
	seventeen point four
	seventeen point four and a quarter
	seventeen point four and a half
	seventeen point four and three quarters
	seventeen point five


		-Joe
--
