Carl R. Friend (carl.friend@prescienttech.com) wrote:
: Ric Werme wrote:
: > 
: > The Packard Bell 250 used blue-green electroluminescent lights.

:    One Volt AC for the filament and 50 VDC for the plate and a grid
: to control the output.

Probaby what we call a DM160 in the UK -- a subminiature indicator valve 
that was used as a logic level indicator on a number of 1960's-ish 
computer and peripherals. The needed a change in grid voltage of about 3V 
to turn them on/off, so they interface easily to most forms of 
transistorised logic.

According to my handy book of valve (tube) equivalents, a DM160 is also a 
6977, a CV5412 and a CV6094

-tony




