 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com

	--

  As for the AlphaStation 500 series...
  
  Power down the system, using appropriate static-prevention steps... 
  
  To enable the failsafe loader, there is a row of jumpers next to the
  SIMM slots, jumpers J11, J12, J13, J14, J15, J16, J17, and (surprise)
  J19.  J11 is furthest from the I/O connectors, and J19 closest... 
  
  J13 is the failsafe loader jumper.
  
  Load a firmware floppy (see the FAQ) into the DVA0: floppy drive. 
  
  Power up the box.
  
  At the UPD> prompt, enter the command sequence:
  
    UPD> update
  
    update SRM: Yes
  
    update ARC: Yes
  
    UPD> verify
  
    UPD> exit
  
  Power down the system, reset the jumper, and power up to reload the
  system with the new firmware the above sequence loaded from the floppy. 
  
  The above information is usually documented in the Owner's Guide for
  the particular box...  (Assuming the particular box does not require
  swapping out the motherboard, of course...)
  




