The DEClaser 1152 should not need to be told anything special to recognize 
input from the parallel port.  But just in case, can you try to print to it 
from a serial port?  

There are three ways to work with this printer: parallel, serial, and
Macintosh serial.  All three should be available anytime.  The protocol used
for any particular port can be set up as either PostScript or HP PCL. 

If you attempt to print PostScript to a port that only recognizes PCL, you
will get pages of PostScript text printed out.  If you try to send HP PCL to a
port configured for PostScript, it will print absolutely nothing.  In either
case, you should see the LED flashing when data is present. 

One other possibility (doesn't seem likely, given your reported symptoms) is
that somehow you may have gotten the PostScript interpreter locked with a
password set.  There were reports a few years ago of some malware that did
this. 

I take it from the wording of your request that you have no manuals for this 
printer.  Let me know if you absolutely have to see some printed pages from 
the manual and I will see if I can help you out.

Alan

