Hi Tim,

I agree with with you in the point, that the
tape path or the loading is not more complicated
due to the fact of 1 tape roll, but i personally had
several times errors on DLT drives with defective
leader tapes(this is the stripe that actually pulls out
the beginning of the tape from the cartridge).
I prefer systems with 2 tape rolls in our application,
because of the fact it loads and unloads MUCH faster
(<10sec), and you can unload it at "special areas"
without rewinding to the beginning. This saves a
consiberable amount of time when you use it for
random access.
If you do only backups these points may not count
for you, but it�s absolutely crucial for HSM style
operations.

cheers
Robert Schmoelzer
Telemed Communications Services, Austria

PS - for Peter: Of course there is a "next generation" DLT,
the long awaited Super-DLT, which should be
available "later this year". At least, this was the
timeframe i got from Storageworks engineering
folks last week.



