>
> My two bits:
>
> I've been inside tape drives after they've eaten tapes.  Everything
> from paper tape to 9-track to 3480's and 3490's to TK50's, DLT, 4mm,
> and 8mm drives.
>
> Your "2 tape roll" vs "1 tape roll" conclusion is fully backwards.  I
> looked at the Qualstar site you mentioned, and their take on this
> issue is technically wrong.  They make it sound like the DLT loading
> mechanism is complicated, when it isn't; they make the tape path
> of a helical scan drive sound simple and reliable, which it isn't.
