Most people would use ftp in binary mode to transfer such a file.  You,
of course, would need a TCP/IP stack on your VMS machine and
software on your Unix machine that understands RMS Indexed files.

Another solution would be to use the DCL CONVERT command on
VMS to convert the file from indexed to sequential before moving it
to the Unix machine (ftp again) where you write a program or use an
existing utility to process the RMS sequential file records, which may
be fixed length records or several different formats of variable length
records.  Then of course you may have binary data in your records,
which need to be processed/converted also.  This can be particularly
problematic if you have VAX native floating point data or packed
decimal data.

If I were doing it, I would convert my VMS file to contain all text data
in an RMS sequential file and then copy it (ftp in text mode) to the
Unix machine.

