>re: DEC 3000 300LX PE32A-C0
>Anyone have any idea what I must do to use the serial port for
a display
>to an emulator on another system.

The "printer" port _does_ work with a PC-based terminal emulator
such as CRT from http://www.vandyke.com/ (shareware, month's
free trial). Use a DB25 to DB9 converter plug/cable, or make up
a cable wiring pins 2-2, 3-3, and 5(DB9)-7(DB25). Turn off all
DSR, DTR, etc. handshaking on the PC and turn on XOFF/XON. If
nothing happens, try swapping connections to pins 2 & 3 at one
end of the cable, or insert a "null modem".

>Is the serial/printer shared on the same connection?

Once you've logged into it as an interactive terminal, that's
what it is, though your terminal emulator may provide ways to
"print through".

>My worry is that the pinouts are vastly different than the PC
arrangement.

Well, not really, since DECpaq only use 3 wires.

Chris

