Alfred Falk <falk@arc.ab.ca> writes:
> Nope.  SCSI.  serial ports block uses 36-pin.  Most likely Phillip Helbig 
> has a VAX 4000-10xA, which has SCSI + dual DSSI, and DB-50 socket/plug 
> pair for external Q-Bus cabinet.

  Nope yerself 8-)

  CXA16-type serial ports (no modem control) use the 36-pin connectors
for 8 serial lines (8 sets of TX+, TX-, RX+, RX- plus 4 uncommitted pins).

  But CXY08-type ports use the 50-pin connectors (for 4 ports w/ full modem
control).

  The MicroVAX 3100 systems have the latter connector on them (but it's a
no-op unless the serial controller daughterboard is installed).

