        These are old dial-in modems of  a  type  that I don't know much
    about  (we  just threw out a similar one).  In the "old days",  when
    you had DEC hardware support (and there weren't very many 3rd  party
    support outfits), DEC would install one of these on your system.  In
    the  event  of  a  crash  or  hang, they could dial in and be at the
    console (assuming  you'd  put  the  selector  switch  in  the proper
    position).   That  was  nice, but it was also  pretty  damned  slow,
    especially by today's standards!

        Other than display it in a computer museum, I doubt there's much
    useful you can do with it...

