Has anyone experienced frequent failures with tlz07 4mm tape drives?  We
have 5 on two scsi buses attached to a single controler that go down in
sets.  The binary error log will show anywhere from 3 to 3 dozen scsi
errors, and the vdumps will get 1-5 i/o errors and abort.  We've swapped
all the drives now, some multiple times.

One item I did notice in the SBB User Guide that comes with the
replacement drives is that the SBB connects have a limited lifespan of
200 connections.  Has anyone run into this as an issue, where replacing
the connectors into which the tapes are plugged having aleviated
problems?

Finally, the man pages for vdump state the this is the selected backup
tool, and the Alpha comes with 4mm drives.  Yet we've been told by the
FE's that we are "over utilizing the tape drives" because we run about
50 different vdumps nightly to backup the various file systems (we've
about 3/4 of a terrabyte of disk).  So this immediate begs the question,
how else are we supposed to do backups?  Any suggestions?

--
Mark
