     about 12-18 months ago we had major problems with a couple of sites
getting bad refurb TLZ06 and TLZ07 DAT drives; the originals had lasted
for quite a few years with no problem, but when DEC installed replace-
ments that were refurbed they would either be DOA or would fail in a 
matter of hours, usually killing the tapes that had been used in them.
Others I asked at that time were having similar results.  DEC ended 
up replacing all of them with refurb'd TLZ09 drives, which have 
provided stellar service since then.  If you are getting Field Service
replacements, maybe the problem is still in existence...

     You know, if I had that much storage to worry about backing up
I think that I'd be looking at DLTs instead of DAT...

