I believe it's a jumper option whether they spin up first. At least
for SCSI disks dkdriver emits scsi START to spin up the drives. This
is done to avoid huge power load at power on. io$_packack causes the
scsi START to be sent as an early part of the processing. This
function is issued at mount time.

