HerbalGypsy/justbobthebard wrote:

> is this the same as the one on the vaxstations using the mono graphics
> interface???
> thanks
> bob

No,
The early VAXstations 2000 and 3100 with monochrome graphics is different
from from the 15 pin connector for keyboard and mouse on DEC 3000 models.

I have a cable from a DEC 5000/240   a MIPS  which has the same cable as
DEC 3000/300 and 3000/400 and ...

The pinout for the 15 pin connector on DEC 3000 Alphas for Keyboard/ Mouse:
Pin   Signal    Description
1     GND       Chassis ground
2     KEY.TX    Keyboard transmitted data  (from computer to keyboard)
3     KEY.RX    Keyboard recieved data  (from keyboard to computer)
4     +12V      Keyboard power
5     GND       Chassis ground
6     MSE.RX    Mouse recieved data  (from mouse to computer)
7     MSE.TX    Mouse transmitted data  (from computer to mouse)
8     GND       Chassis ground
9     GND       Chassis ground
10    NC        Not used
10    NC        Not used
10    NC        Not used
13    +5V       Mouse power
14    -12V      Mouse power
15    GND       Chassis ground

Now you only need the pinout of the 4/4 modular connector on the keyboard.
It is the same on all Vax and Alphas and VT terminals (except VT100).

Try to download
  http://www.europe.digital.com/alphaserver/archive/axp/dec3000.pdf
It is a large .pdf document containing the
owners manual for DEC 3000 model 600 alpha.
Except for hardware details, a lot of the descriptions in there is valid also for
your 3000 model 300.

Have luck

Arne Bergseth





