The VAXstation 2000 had an RX33 floppy disk drive.  It could handle RX-50
and RX33 (standard Hi-density formatted) media.

All of the RX50 media that I have seen has RX-50 somewhere prominently on
the label somewhere.

See the VMS freeware CD available at a link from
http://www.openvms.digital.com and other places for a program that can read
ODS-2 from a MS-DOS PC.  There also seems to be one on the www that will
work on LINUX.

ODS-2 is the way that VMS will likely have formatted the disk.  They could
also be ODS-1 format though.

