In article <38e7c2b1$1@news>, "Ram Rajadhyaksha"
<ramr@dlzcorp.com> wrote:
..
>TXA3 originally was used as a printer queue. I deleted the
queue associated
>with it, etc. I then tried configuring the speed and other
terminal attributes
>via the SET TERM command, but no matter what I do, I can't get
the thing to
>work. The terminal device on connected to the end of the cable
never shows a
>login prompt.

Does SHOT TERMINAL TXA� say "Owner: No owner"? If not, maybe you
haven't really stopped the queue.

Anyway, TXA3's probably SET /NOTYPEHEAD to stop the printer (or
noise on the line) attempting to log in. Find a line that _does_
log in and SET every option on TXA3 the same as that one. Don't
forget the /PERMANENT qualifier (from a suitably privileged
account, such as SYSTEM). You may also have to do a SHOW
DEVICE/FULL on TXA3/TXA<working> and issue appropriate SET
commands.

Search SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM and any command procedure
files it invokes for any command that sets up TXA3 on system
startup and remove them or make them the same as TXA<working>.

Chris

