Are you sure it is a 3100 and not a 3000-xxx series?
I've never seen a 3100, but I have seen 3000's with the little box for the
keyboard and mouse, and I actually have one.  However, I have never seen the
little box fail. The most likely failure is the mouse or keyboard.  I've
also had systems where the IO board (resides on top of mother board with all
the connections to the outside world) has failed.
Pin outs won't help much, unless you try to substitute similar but different
devices.  I'd first try swapping mice and keyboards, then the IO board.
I buy all my DEC stuff from Don at Hess Electronics, (714) 669-9838, he's
located in Southern California.
