I have a TLZ06 drive in an HP 715/100XC.  I know, I know, I'm mixing
vendors.  *slaps himself on the wrist*  But it's worked in the past, and in
fact was working until very recently.

It stopped working with no warning; it simply refused to eject the tape that
had been in it for about 14 runs.  (This is my home machine.  I'm a little
sloppy about my tape rotation.  :) Both amber and green lights flashed twice
at power-on, but it still refused to eject.  Oh, and it also stopped
responding on the SCSI bus at the same time.

After a bit of messing, I figured out that holding the eject button whilst
powering on allowed me to eject the tape, and it now functions *almost*
normally -- shows up on the bus and everything.

I say almost because it doesn't actually load the tape.  It sucks it up and
clicks a bit, flashes the amber light once, then goes dark.  It ejects just
fine.  But I know it's not really loaded, because it ejects much too quickly
(this drive usually takes 20 seconds to unload a tape).

I can't figure out what's wrong.  At powerup, both lights flash together,
nine times.  When loading a tape, the amber light flashes once.  When
ejecting, the sequence is amber - green - green - green.  Tapping (not
holding) the eject button with a tape "loaded" gives amber - green - amber -
green - amber.

I have absolutely NO IDEA what the lights mean.  I only know that during a
successful load, it flashes green several times.  I haven't seen that in
weeks.

My suspicions are:
1. The drive is fubar and I should get a decent drive anyways.
2. The drive is misaligned and therefore can't load a tape now.
3. The drive needs some kind of reset.
4. The drive needs to be cleaned.  (Prolly does anyways :)

Any ideas?

Hal



