  Mach64s are hit-or-miss.  The GX chip had so much flexibility in how it
was configured
  in terms of memory, RAMDAC, and clocks -- that you can easily find one
that will not
  initialize on Tru64 UNIX or VMS.  The Trio64 on the other hand is a simple
stupid single
  chip solution (like the Mach64-CT) and the only variable is really how
much memory is
  on it.

  As to the ELSA, anything with a 3DLabs P2A chip in it should work... and
later versions
  of the ELSA code also support the P2V.







