I've nearly always made my own.  The crimping tool for the MMJ may seem
a bit pricey but well work the price if you do this alot.  I purchased
one with interchangeable dies for MMJ, RJ-11, RJ45, various RG BNC, etc.
in a kit which was about $70.00 - $80.00 (As part of a promotion.  They
are typically more costly).  

The MMJ plugs can be purchased for a few cents and a spool of flat 6 wire
cable is a couple of bucks.  

I like to make my own because I make the cable to the exact length I'll
need and don't have to clutter up the work space with rubber-banded or
ratchetted wire-tied bundles of excess.

A DataComm warehouse catalog which stuffed the mailbox yesterday has a
similar Paladin Tool kit with all of the dies for $89.00.  No affili-
ation with DataComm or Paladin -- just a handy catalog within reach.

