In article <38e4a1eb.14923353@news.conceptsfa.nl>, stefan@softhome.net (Stefan) writes:
>Are the pathworks free to download and if so where can I find them ??
>Because I thought they were on the Windows CD but you need the
>original disks.

1) PATHWORKS for OpenVMS was renamed with V7 to Advanced Server for OpenVMS.
It is not free, not downloadable and the homepage is

http://www.openvms.digital.com/pathworks/		currently V6.0C
http://www.openvms.digital.com/advancedserver/		currently V7.2A

ECOs can (sometimes) be found on http://www.service.digital.com/


2) PATHWORKS for Tru64 UNIX was renamed some time ago to Advanced Server
for UNIX, too. I don't know details.


3) So what now only is called PATHWORKS is the client software PATHWORKS-32.
It is not free, not downloadable and the homepage is

http://www.openvms.digital.com/pathworks32/		currently V7.1A

It consists of 3 parts:
	*) Networks drivers for Win32	=> DECnet and LAT
	*) eXcursion for Win32		=> X11 server
	*) PowerTerm525	for Win32	=> VT525 emulator

ECOs can be found on the PATHWORKS-32 homepage.

So, you only need PATHWORKS-32 if you insist on running DECnet and/or LAT
instead of TCP/IP or if you have a need for an X11 server and a terminal
emulator (PATHWORKS-32 package is good [enough] and much cheaper than other
X11 server for Win32 and/or terminal emulator products)


Currently, there is a beta version of PATHWORKS-32 V7.2 (w/ W2K support)
downloadable on the PATHWORKS-32 homepage. You might give it a try...

