In article <38E4D4D0.4A8CD54F@americasm01.nt.com>,
Blasutti, Bob [CAR:5Z63:EXCH] <blasutti@americasm01.nt.com> wrote:
>"Blasutti, Bob [CAR:5Z63:EXCH]" wrote:
>> This may be a bizarre question...
>>
>> Does anyone know if typical UNIX remote access daemons (telnet, rlogin, rsh,
>> etc)
>> will work with a Radius server?
>> For example, radius client support built into the UNIX telnet server?
>
>Anyone know if there is a PAM module available for
>Compaq's (Digital) Tru64 Unix?


PAM is relatively low-level stuff, it's only really useful if they have
built all of the system standard daemons that need to authenticate passwords
linked against their standard PAM library, which is what Solaris did in their
2.6 release.

If you don't see any man pages for PAM in a standard Tru64 install, it's
most likely not part of Digital's Unix. If you just need RADIUS authentication
for telnet, rlogin, and FTP, you could replace the standard binaries with
ones compiled from public sources.

One option would be to use the free TIS 'Firewall Toolkit' (FWTK) to build
the FTPd and a telnetd wrapper on Tru64, set to use the TIS authentication
protocol and authenticate against a TIS Gauntlet firewall running RADIUS.

			http://www.fwtk.org/
			http://www.pgp.com/asp_set/products/tns/gauntlet.asp



